ogles2: half-float and float textures on VC4 (docs/PI3_PLAN.md §2.1,
OES_texture_half_float, OES_texture_float). A sampler keyed
PIPE_FORMAT_R16G16B16A16_FLOAT reads four planes of the S16F texture type,
one a channel, each a whole miptree the TMU filters: four lookups, the
uniform recipe's P0 data word carrying the plane in bits 16 and up (the
library adds that plane's offset; Mesa's own P0 writer masks it off), each
result's half in the word's low 16 bits (the 16a float unpack). Not the
RGBA64 type, which reads one request as two words (RG, BA): on the Pi 3 its
second word came back stale, from earlier lookups, once a 32-bit texture
had been sampled since the core's reset (PI3_PLAN §2 "Textures",
2026-11-05). The texture request is split out of ntq_emit_tex
(ntq_tex_request) for the four. Mesa's vc4 has no such textures (its format
table lacks the format), so no draw of Mesa's own makes this key: v3dglslc
compiles it from keys (-k, patch 0017). Applies after 0017.

